  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "Given a quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) inscribed in a circle with side \\(AB\\) extended beyond \\(B\\) to point \\(E,\\) if \\(\\angle BAD=92^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle ADC=68^\\circ,\\) find \\(\\angle EBC.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(66^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(68^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(70^\\circ\\)",
    "D": "\\(88^\\circ\\)",
    "E": "\\(92^\\circ\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The given angle at \\(D\\) is opposite the angle at \\(B\\). Opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary, so\n\\[\n\\angle ABC=180^\\circ-68^\\circ=112^\\circ.\n\\]\nSince \\(AB\\) is extended beyond \\(B\\) to \\(E\\), rays \\(BA\\) and \\(BE\\) point in opposite directions. Hence \\(\\angle ABC\\) and \\(\\angle EBC\\) are also supplementary. Therefore\n\\[\n\\angle EBC=180^\\circ-112^\\circ=\\boxed{68^\\circ},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
